{"id":"gaal","name":"Gaal","aliases":[],"sources":["nave","easton"],"topics":["nave:gaal"],"groups":[],"definition":{"source":"easton","term":"Gaal","text":"Loathing, the son of Ebed, in whom the Shechemites “placed their confidence” when they became discontented with Abimelech. He headed the revolution, and led out the men of Shechem against Abimelech; but was defeated, and fled to his own home (Judg. 9:26-46). We hear no more of him after this battle."},"lemmas":[{"strong":"H1603","lemma":"גַּעַל","xlit":"Gaʻal","gloss":"Gaal, an Israelite","kjv":"Gaal","count":9,"share":0.56},{"strong":"H40","lemma":"אֲבִימֶלֶךְ","xlit":"ʼĂbîymelek","gloss":"Abimelek, the name of two Philistine kings and of two Is","kjv":"Abimelech","count":10,"share":0.63},{"strong":"H2083","lemma":"זְבֻל","xlit":"Zᵉbul","gloss":"Zebul, an Israelite","kjv":"Zebul","count":5,"share":0.31},{"strong":"H5651","lemma":"עֶבֶד","xlit":"ʻEbed","gloss":"Ebed, the name of two Israelites","kjv":"Ebed","count":5,"share":0.31},{"strong":"H7927","lemma":"שְׁכֶם","xlit":"Shᵉkem","gloss":"Shekem, a place in Palestine","kjv":"Shechem","count":6,"share":0.38},{"strong":"H693","lemma":"אָרַב","xlit":"ʼârab","gloss":"to lurk","kjv":"ambush, lay  wait","count":2,"share":0.13}],"verses":["Judg.9.26","Judg.9.28","Judg.9.30","Judg.9.31","Judg.9.35","Judg.9.36","Judg.9.37","Judg.9.39","Judg.9.41","Judg.9.27","Judg.9.29","Judg.9.32","Judg.9.33","Judg.9.34","Judg.9.38","Judg.9.40"],"related":[{"id":"zebul","type":"cooccur","shared":14,"jaccard":0.875,"why":"14 verses are indexed under both"},{"id":"ebed","type":"cooccur","shared":10,"jaccard":0.588,"why":"10 verses are indexed under both"},{"id":"conspiracy","type":"cooccur","shared":16,"jaccard":0.082,"why":"16 verses are indexed under both"},{"id":"judge","type":"cooccur","shared":15,"jaccard":0.055,"why":"15 verses are indexed under both"},{"id":"ebed","type":"lexical","strong":"H1603","why":"both lead with גַּעַל (H1603)"},{"id":"zebul","type":"lexical","strong":"H160